# The fist: a jab, twice in a row; the third use within the combo's window is a finisher. A press
# starts the punch (the pack, brawl.fists, plays it); the hit is where the fist lands: the clip's
# brawl.fist.strike marker. Whoever is in the box where the player looks then (2.6 m ahead, knee to
# head height) is hit (said with who it was: the brawl mod's damage) and pushed. The punch is over
# at the clip's brawl.fist.ready marker (the fist mostly back): until then the next one cannot start,
# so spamming plays whole punches.
# Without the markers (a body the pack does not fit, a server without the pack) the punch lands a
# moment later anyway: the "within" gives up and its timeout hits the same way.

motion Jab on use if not linked and brawl.combo < 2 and not motion.brawl.fist.Finisher
	cooldown 0.3
	change brawl.combo += 1
	change brawl.combo_left = 1.5
	then when brawl.fist.strike within 0.35
	find box (0.8, 1.2, 2.6) at (0, 1, 1.4) max 1 turned look
		emit brawl.jab.hit
		impulse 4 along move
	timeout
	find box (0.8, 1.2, 2.6) at (0, 1, 1.4) max 1 turned look
		emit brawl.jab.hit
		impulse 4 along move
	then when brawl.fist.ready within 0.7

motion Finisher on use if brawl.combo >= 2 and not motion.brawl.fist.Jab
	cooldown 0.3
	change brawl.combo = 0
	then when brawl.fist.strike within 0.5
	find box (0.8, 1.2, 2.6) at (0, 1, 1.4) max 1 turned look
		emit brawl.finisher.hit
		impulse 14 along move
		impulse 5 along up
	timeout
	find box (0.8, 1.2, 2.6) at (0, 1, 1.4) max 1 turned look
		emit brawl.finisher.hit
		impulse 14 along move
		impulse 5 along up
	then when brawl.fist.ready within 0.9
